      "quote": "A future experiment could hold each verified history fixed and randomise an advisor-only display, a paired display, or a selection-adjusted paired display. It would also randomise uniform versus high-confidence disagreement selection and provide an explicit marginal self-accuracy benchmark.",
      "feedback": "I initially read “hold each verified history fixed” as applying across both randomisations. That cannot test the effect of selection: if the same cases are verified under both policies, the displayed evidence has the same distribution, regardless of which policy label is assigned. The intended design seems to hold a verified history fixed across displays within each selection condition, but the passage does not specify that distinction. It matters because the predicted interaction depends on selection changing which disagreement outcomes are revealed. Rewrite “hold each verified history fixed” as “hold the encountered cases fixed across selection conditions, generate verified histories under the assigned selection rules, and hold each verified history fixed across display conditions” because the selection rules must be allowed to produce different observed histories.",
      "status": "Pending",
